{
 "_source": "What each Enchanting material is worth, in copper, for costing the Enchanting route (scripts/professions/cheapest-route.mjs enchanting). Captured 2026-10-18 from the 1.60.1 beta datamine.",
 "_how": "A material is worth what you give up to get it: the price of an item you would otherwise sell, divided by how many of that material disenchanting it gives on average. For each material the cheapest source wins: green armor (mostly dust), green weapons (mostly essences) or blues (shards) of any item-level band. A material in 'overrides' takes that price instead, and a material a vendor sells is never worth more than its vendor price. To revalue the route, edit 'itemPrices' (e.g. with auction-house prices of greens and blues) or 'overrides' (e.g. with auction-house prices of the materials themselves) and rerun the script.",
